{
  "requirement": "The SDK MUST expose a source-provider interface through which an application\ncan enumerate resource identities within a requested scope and read a resource's\nbytes. The interface MUST support resources that have no local filesystem path.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.sources.provider`**\n1. The SDK exposes a provider interface that enumerates resource identities within a requested scope.\n2. The same interface reads a resource's bytes.\n3. The interface supports resources that have no local filesystem path.\n\nThe `{impl}` site is `crates/habeas-sdk/src/sources.rs#trait[SourceProvider]`. Its required methods are `list(&SourceScope) -> Vec<ResourceId>` and `read(&ResourceId) -> SourceFile`.\n\n**Marked test:** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/sources.rs#fn[defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot]`\n\n- **Resources with no local path (obligation 3).** The test uses the `Memory` provider, which implements `SourceProvider`. Its `ResourceId`s have scheme `memory` and a logical location such as `src/one.txt`. No filesystem path is involved. The bytes are synthesized in `read`.\n- **Reading bytes (obligation 2).**\n  - `memory.parse` reads `src/one.txt` through the provider, and the test asserts the text starts with the first version marker.\n  - A direct `memory.read` returns the next version. This shows the bytes come from the provider's `read` and are not cached.\n  - The read counter and the event log assert how many reads happened and which resources were read.\n- **Enumerating within a scope (obligation 1).**\n  - `search_text` is called with `SourceScope { prefix: \"src\" }`. It goes through `list`, which the event log records as `list`.\n  - `Memory::list` returns both `src/one.txt` and `other/two.txt`. The event log shows that only `src/one.txt` is read afterwards, so the scoped enumeration result was used.\n  - The asserted matches (count, line and excerpt) confirm the bytes were read and searched.\n\n**Supporting tests without a `{test}` reference to the subject**\n- `local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root` calls `list` directly with the default scope and with `src`. It asserts the listed identities and reads a listed identity's bytes.\n- `successful_empty_listing_and_empty_resources_are_distinct_from_errors` also calls `list` and `read` directly on a test provider.\n\nThese tests are not marked for this requirement. They add confidence but are not needed to cover it, so I did not treat them as a gap.\n\n**Gap check:** I found no plausible violation that these tests would accept. Both `list` and `read` are required trait methods, and both are exercised with a non-filesystem provider. Scope is passed to `list` and observably affects which resources get read. Errors, defaults and parse snapshots are covered by other requirements and are not assessed here. There is no `{fixme}` acknowledgment.",
  "references": "1a40e3f08c3f8b9c4f83d58603de36056a9957734b574473b139371f99b6f6e1",
